    },
    {
      "id": "zvqNJSnkzaAIRD0ZMe2iG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2366.412551168348,
      "y": -2221.246118057887,
      "width": 530.5507702389807,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1352494386,
      "version": 197,
      "versionNonce": 472265724,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784610303419,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "=> We can keep one istance of DB since \n    modern day SSDs can hold >=100 TBs of data",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "=> We can keep one istance of DB since \n    modern day SSDs can hold >=100 TBs of data",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZE2oj7KDOCUsckHj2V7Fq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2207.2688448486992,
      "y": -1304.8936720518154,
      "width": 445.6196594238281,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0t",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1227498158,
      "version": 345,
      "versionNonce": 1199839684,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784610303419,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n=> Counter : redis high availability mode \n    / store a snapshot in disk periodically\n    to cater the high availability requirement)\n\n    Database : For high availability we can\n    have single replica and a periodic snapshot\n    stored in S3 ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n=> Counter : redis high availability mode \n    / store a snapshot in disk periodically\n    to cater the high availability requirement)\n\n    Database : For high availability we can\n    have single replica and a periodic snapshot\n    stored in S3 ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "GSvdNzPFmU2ff900EEYAP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 707.1713886049353,
      "y": -186.39620154436398,
      "width": 686.0795288085938,
      "height": 1375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1609574524,
      "version": 1032,
      "versionNonce": 976967748,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784612359424,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design an ad-click aggregator\n\n\nFunctional requirements : \n    - Users click an ad and get redirected to the advertiser's website \n    - Advertisers can query click metrics over time w/1 min. granularity \n\n--- out of scope --- \n- Ad targeting & serving \n- Cross device tracking \n- Integration with offline channels \n\n\n10M ads at any given time \n10k ad clicks per second at its peak\n\n\nNon-functional\n- Scalable to support 10k CPS \n- Low latency analytics queries <1s\n- Fault tolerance \n- Data integrity\n- As realtime as possible\n- Idempotency of ad clicks \n\n---out of scope---\n- Spam detection\n- Demographic profiling \n- Conversion tracking\n   \n\nInput :\n- Click Data\n- Advertiser Queries \n\nOutputs :\n- Redirection \n- Aggregated click Metrics\n\n\n\nData Flow :\n\n1. Click data comes into the system\n2. User is redirected \n3. Click data validated\n4. Click data logged\n5. Click data aggregated\n6. Aggregated data queried\n\n \n \n \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design an ad-click aggregator\n\n\nFunctional requirements : \n    - Users click an ad and get redirected to the advertiser's website \n    - Advertisers can query click metrics over time w/1 min. granularity \n\n--- out of scope --- \n- Ad targeting & serving \n- Cross device tracking \n- Integration with offline channels \n\n\n10M ads at any given time \n10k ad clicks per second at its peak\n\n\nNon-functional\n- Scalable to support 10k CPS \n- Low latency analytics queries <1s\n- Fault tolerance \n- Data integrity\n- As realtime as possible\n- Idempotency of ad clicks \n\n---out of scope---\n- Spam detection\n- Demographic profiling \n- Conversion tracking\n   \n\nInput :\n- Click Data\n- Advertiser Queries \n\nOutputs :\n- Redirection \n- Aggregated click Metrics\n\n\n\nData Flow :\n\n1. Click data comes into the system\n2. User is redirected \n3. Click data validated\n4. Click data logged\n5. Click data aggregated\n6. Aggregated data queried\n\n \n \n \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
